### Model Buildup (Mid Tier, R2)

Pre-storm trend is the only significant predictor across all specifications (`r pre_trend_coef`). Coastal becomes significant in the full specification (`r coastal_coef`), separating the specific effect of coastal location from NRI counterparts. Log damage, log income, log population density, NRI risk value, expected annual loss, resilience, and social vulnerability are all insignificant. Within R² is essentially flat from M1 to M5 (`r m1_r2w*100`% to `r m5_r2w*100`%) storm and NRI variables add negligible explanatory power beyond pre-trend. The pre-trend coefficient implies strong mean reversion. Counties underperforming before the storm outperform after, regardless of storm characteristics.

### Baseline Sensitivity (Mid Tier, Preferred Spec)

Pre-trend coefficient varies by baseline: Regional (`r pre_trend_regional`) \> R2 (`r pre_trend_l2`) \> R1 (`r pre_trend_l1`), all significant at 1%. Coastal is significant only on R2 (`r coastal_l2`\*\*). Regional shows same direction (`r coastal_regional`) but wider SE. R1 shows no effect (`r coastal_l1`). NRI Risk Value approaches significance on R1 only (`r risk_l1`\*) with N=`r format(n_obs_l1, big.mark=",")`. Within R² ranges from `r r2w_l1`% (R1) to `r r2w_regional`% (Regional). No other variable reaches significance on any baseline. The null result on NRI risk value is robust to baseline choices.

### Tier Comparison (R2, Preferred Spec)

Pre-trend significant and similar across all tiers (`r pre_trend_top` to `r pre_trend_mid`\*\*\*). Coastal significant on mid (`r coastal_mid`\*\*), but not bottom (`r coastal_bottom`\*) or top (`r coastal_top`). Log damage approaches significance on bottom tier only (`r damage_bottom`\*). Damage is associated with price depreciation in the lowest market segment. NRI risk coefficient varies across tiers, the null effect is robust across market segments. NRI does not capture tier-specific vulnerability. Within R² is highest on bottom tier (`r r2w_bottom`%) and lowest on top (`r r2w_top`%). Storm characteristics explain slightly more variance in financially vulnerable markets.

